{"name":"Heron","hex":"#6a6887","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Heron","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A surname.","A census-designated place in Sanders County, Montana, United States."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Heron"}],"entries":[{"title":"Heron","blocks":[{"text":"Herons are long-legged, long-necked, freshwater and coastal birds in the family Ardeidae, with 75 recognised species, some of which are referred to as egrets or bitterns rather than herons. Members of the genus Botaurus are referred to as bitterns, and, together with the zigzag heron, or zigzag bittern, in the monotypic genus Zebrilus, form a monophyletic group, Botaurinae, within the Ardeidae family. Egrets do not form a biologically distinct group from herons, and tend to be named differently because they are mainly white or have decorative plumes in breeding plumage. Herons, by evolutionary adaptation, have long beaks."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9e/Ardeidae-01.jpg/330px-Ardeidae-01.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Heron","wikidata":"Q18789"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bc/Goliath_heron_standing_cropped.jpg/500px-Goliath_heron_standing_cropped.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bc/Goliath_heron_standing_cropped.jpg/500px-Goliath_heron_standing_cropped.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The goliath heron is the largest heron species.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGoliath_heron_standing_cropped.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/33/Yellow_Bittern_hunting.jpg/500px-Yellow_Bittern_hunting.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/33/Yellow_Bittern_hunting.jpg/500px-Yellow_Bittern_hunting.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Yellow bittern with its neck fully retracted.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AYellow_Bittern_hunting.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/26/Cervical_vertebrae_in_the_neck_of_a_heron_%28X-ray%29.jpg/500px-Cervical_vertebrae_in_the_neck_of_a_heron_%28X-ray%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/26/Cervical_vertebrae_in_the_neck_of_a_heron_%28X-ray%29.jpg/500px-Cervical_vertebrae_in_the_neck_of_a_heron_%28X-ray%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"X-ray of the cervical vertebrae in the neck of an unidentified heron","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACervical_vertebrae_in_the_neck_of_a_heron_(X-ray).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/65/Eastern_reef_egrets_in_Ko_Tao.jpg/500px-Eastern_reef_egrets_in_Ko_Tao.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/65/Eastern_reef_egrets_in_Ko_Tao.jpg/1280px-Eastern_reef_egrets_in_Ko_Tao.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/65/Eastern_reef_egrets_in_Ko_Tao.jpg/500px-Eastern_reef_egrets_in_Ko_Tao.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The Pacific reef heron has two colour morphs, the light and the dark.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AEastern_reef_egrets_in_Ko_Tao.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c9/White_Heron_Closeup.jpg/500px-White_Heron_Closeup.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, http